<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
    Vozidlo watch app manifest.

    type="watch-app", API level 5.2, see docs/best-practices/garmin-connect-iq.md,
    section "Scope".

    Products: every one is device family round-260x260 with a watch-app budget
    of 786,432 B and a glance budget of 65,536 B, so one set of layouts covers
    all of them and ControlsView's fixed 260x260 grid needs no rework. This is
    read from each device's own compiler.json, not inferred from model names.

      fenix7pro           fēnix® 7 Pro. Per the store's Compatible Devices list
                          this one id covers four retail SKUs: 7 Pro, 7 Pro
                          Solar, 7 Pro Sapphire Solar and 7 Pro Sapphire Dual
                          Power. Listed FIRST because tools/ciq treats the first
                          product as the primary: the one `build`, `run` and
                          `test` use by default, and that should be the watch
                          we can actually put this on.
      fenix7              fēnix® 7 / quatix® 7 / 7 Sapphire Dual Power.
      fenix7pronowifi     fēnix® 7 Pro - Solar Edition (no Wi-Fi).
      fenix8solar47mm     fēnix® 8 Solar 47mm. Connect IQ 6.0.2.
      fenix9prosolar47mm  fēnix® 9 Pro Solar 47mm. Connect IQ 6.0.3.
      fr955               Forerunner® 955 / 955 Solar.

    Every one of these carries the full implementation of all four APIs this app
    needs, checked against each device's own <device>.api.debug.xml, not
    assumed: WatchUi.MapView, Toybox.Complications, Toybox.PersistedContent and
    WatchUi.GlanceView.

    DELIBERATELY EXCLUDED, and why, so nobody re-adds them by accident:

      fr255, fr255m       Forerunner® 255 / 255 Music. Same family, same
                          Connect IQ version, and they BUILD CLEAN at -l 3 -w,
                          which is exactly the trap. Their api.debug.xml has
                          zero Toybox_WatchUi_MapView entries against nine on
                          every device above: the type resolves, the
                          implementation is absent. These watches have no
                          onboard maps. ui/MapPreviewView.mc extends
                          WatchUi.MapView at class level, so a green build says
                          nothing about whether it loads. Compare the glance
                          crash, which also compiled.
      fenix6, fenix6pro,  Connect IQ 3.x, below our minApiLevel of 5.2.0, and
      vivoactive4,        fenix6 has a 131,072 B watch-app budget: about half
      approachs62,        what this app needs, with no glance support at all.
      the legacy hero
      and saga watches
      7S / 7X Pro and     240x240 and 280x280. A different device family, so
      the 42/51mm 8, 9    ControlsView's grid would need a real layout pass
                          before we could honestly claim them.
-->
<iq:manifest xmlns:iq="http://www.garmin.com/xml/connectiq" version="3">
    <iq:application id="96a4e892-508e-4772-8a91-2c464b118264" type="watch-app" name="@Strings.AppName" entry="VozidloApp" launcherIcon="@Drawables.LauncherIcon" minApiLevel="5.2.0">
        <iq:products>
            <iq:product id="fenix7pro"/>
            <iq:product id="fenix7"/>
            <iq:product id="fenix7pronowifi"/>
            <iq:product id="fenix8solar47mm"/>
            <iq:product id="fenix9prosolar47mm"/>
            <iq:product id="fr955"/>
        </iq:products>
        <iq:permissions>
            <!--
                Communications: Toybox.Communications, for the REST calls to the
                mock/real Škoda API (task 4).

                Positioning: Toybox.Position, for Find My Car (task 9). The task
                brief names this permission "Positions", but the SDK's actual
                permission id is "Positioning": there is no "Positions" id.
                See doc/docs/Core_Topics/Manifest_and_Permissions.html in the
                Connect IQ SDK.

                ComplicationPublisher: Toybox.Complications, for task 10's four
                published complications (US-038): one <complication> per id in
                resources/complications/complications.xml, updated from
                source/Complications.mc. Confirmed as the correct permission id
                against the SDK's own compiled permission table
                (monkeybrains.jar's projectInfo.xml) rather than trusted from
                the SDK's Manifest_and_Permissions.html doc page alone: that
                page's permission TABLE lists this row as "ComplicationProvider",
                which does not match: the compiler's own permission list, and
                the Complications core-topic guide's worked example, both say
                "ComplicationPublisher". Treated the compiler as authoritative.

                PersistedContent: Toybox.PersistedContent, for Find My Car's
                "Navigate" action (task 9, US-032): PersistedContent.saveWaypoint()/
                getAppWaypoints(). Added here rather than by task 9 itself because
                this file is task 10's alone to edit (see the file-ownership split);
                without it the whole app fails to build, which blocks every task's
                own verification, not only task 9's.
            -->
            <iq:uses-permission id="Communications"/>
            <iq:uses-permission id="Positioning"/>
            <iq:uses-permission id="ComplicationPublisher"/>
            <iq:uses-permission id="PersistedContent"/>
        </iq:permissions>
        <iq:languages>
            <iq:language>eng</iq:language>
        </iq:languages>
        <iq:barrels/>
    </iq:application>
</iq:manifest>
